# Javadoc Style Conventions
* All javadocs are written like a sentence.
  So it had to start with a capital and ends with a full stop.

## Naming conventions
* Class name are written in UpperCamelCase and had a minimum length of 3.
* Method name are written in lowerCamelCase and had a minimum length of 2.
* Parameter and variable name are written in lowerCamelCase and had a minimum length of 3.
* Attributes and  are written in lowercase and had a minimum length of 3.
* Package name are written in lowercase and had a minimum length of 2.

### Acronyms
* Acronyms used in the SRS are allowed.

## Tags
* Every `{@param}` and `{@return}` tag states the values range.
  This include to state if it can be `null` (for object types) and when it does, what that means.
* It is forbitten to add the package when the `{@link}` or `{@see}` tag is uesed.
  Only exepted if it is necessary.